evidence.quote:
Replay proves that the stored inputs, engine version and seed produce the stored metrics on
the same platform family. It does not prove:

- that the model is valid;
- that the inputs are measured;
- that the confidence interval covers a production value;
- that the decision is correct;
- that another platform will produce bit-identical floats.

A job that copies 10,000 source rows and produces 10,000 target rows can still corrupt meanings. Check:
- stable source/target identity and tenant scope;
- field-level semantic equivalence and unknown mappings;
- concurrent writes, deletes and timestamps;
- checkpoint durability on crash/retry;
- event/CDC offset and replay horizon;
- history, authorization and referential integrity;
- exact source snapshot and migration code version.

Return insufficient evidence when any of the following holds:

- a hard input is assumed and its range spans the decision boundary;
- a hard constraint cannot be evaluated by the model;
- the confidence interval includes both a pass and a fail on a decision-relevant metric;
- two candidates are indistinguishable on the declared metrics;
- the model's validity limits exclude the operating condition under test;
- the rollback or recovery path has not been exercised;
- the objective or metric ranking is contested.
